there is a bug when you are holding down a key to move and you accidently click outside of the browser window. the character gets stuck moving 1 direction.

here is a code snippet that will fix the issue at around line 1008. 

window.addEventListener('blur', () => {
    for (const k in keys) keys[k] = false;
    mouseDown.left = false;
    mouseDown.right = false;
});
document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
    if (document.hidden) {
        for (const k in keys) keys[k] = false;
        mouseDown.left = false;
        mouseDown.right = false;
    }
});

Why it happens: the game tracks movement with a keys object set by window.addEventListener('keydown', ...) / keyup (around lines 996–1008), and player movement just reads keys['w'], keys['a'], etc. (lines 1738–1741). If a key is held down and then you click on something outside the browser window (another app, taskbar, a second monitor, an OS dialog), the browser tab loses focus. The keyup event for that key fires on the OS-level target, not on your page — since the window is no longer focused, the page never receives it. So keys['w'] stays true forever, and the sorcerer keeps walking in that direction until you press and release that key again inside the game.


